cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Open-Weight Agent Safety: measurement infrastructure for indirect prompt injection on locally-hosted models"
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the paper below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pachter
    given-names: Ben
repository-code: "https://github.com/bpachter/open-weight-agent-safety"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/bpachter/open-weight-agent-safety/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - indirect prompt injection
  - LLM agents
  - AI safety
  - open-weight models
  - quantization
  - evaluation methodology
  - agent security
abstract: >-
  A factorial measurement harness and trial-level dataset for indirect
  prompt-injection attacks against quantized open-weight language models
  running on a single consumer GPU. Attack success is decomposed into
  delivery, obedience and execution stages rather than reported as a single
  rate, on the grounds that a model too weak to call tools scores near zero
  on the product while having no injection resistance at all. Includes
  negative and active control arms, so measured effects are attributable to
  the injected payload rather than to baseline behaviour.

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Unattacked, Not Unbreakable: Decomposing Prompt-Injection Success in Quantized Open-Weight Agents"
